NNAAMMEE
     iissccssiidd — iSCSI initiator daemon

SSYYNNOOPPSSIISS
     iissccssiidd [--PP _p_i_d_f_i_l_e] [--dd] [--ll _l_o_g_l_e_v_e_l] [--mm _m_a_x_p_r_o_c] [--tt _s_e_c_o_n_d_s]

DDEESSCCRRIIPPTTIIOONN
     The iissccssiidd daemon is the userspace component of the iSCSI initiator, re‐
     sponsible for performing the Login Phase of iSCSI connections and the
     SendTargets discovery.

     Upon startup, the iissccssiidd daemon opens the iSCSI initiator device file and
     waits for requests from the kernel component, iscsi(4).  iissccssiidd does not
     use any configuration files.  All needed information is supplied by the
     kernel.

     When the iissccssiidd daemon is not running, already established iSCSI connec‐
     tions continue to work.  However, establishing new connections, or recov‐
     ering existing ones in case of connection error, is not possible.

     The following options are available:

     --PP _p_i_d_f_i_l_e  Specify alternative location of a file where main process PID
                 will be stored.  The default location is _/_v_a_r_/_r_u_n_/_i_s_c_s_i_d_._p_i_d.

     --dd          Debug mode.  The daemon sends verbose debug output to stan‐
                 dard error, and does not put itself in the background.  The
                 daemon will also not fork and will exit after processing one
                 connection.  This option is only intended for debugging the
                 initiator.

     --ll _l_o_g_l_e_v_e_l
                 Specifies debug level.  The default is 0.

     --mm _m_a_x_p_r_o_c  Specifies limit for concurrently running child processes han‐
                 dling connections.  The default is 30.  Setting it to 0 dis‐
                 ables the limit.

     --tt _s_e_c_o_n_d_s  Specifies timeout for login session, after which the connec‐
                 tion will be forcibly terminated.  The default is 60.  Set‐
                 ting it to 0 disables the timeout.

FFIILLEESS
     /dev/iscsi           The iSCSI initiator device file.
     /var/run/iscsid.pid  The default location of the iissccssiidd PID file.

EEXXIITT SSTTAATTUUSS
     The iissccssiidd utility exits 0 on success, and >0 if an error occurs.

SSEEEE AALLSSOO
     iscsi(4), iscsictl(8)

HHIISSTTOORRYY
     The iissccssiidd command appeared in FreeBSD 10.0.

